---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import EsyohWidget from '../../components/EsyohWidget.astro';
import AiSummary from '../../components/AiSummary.astro';
import { resources } from '../../data/resources';
import { site, teamBySlug } from '../../data/site';
import { outcomesSurvey } from '../../data/research';
import { stats } from '../../data/quality-index';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Nutrition Career and Education Guides"
  description={`${resources.length} long-form guides on nutrition and dietetics education, credentialing, salaries, and career strategy, built on federal data and our own graduate research.`}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Guides and analysis</p>
      <h1>The questions worth answering before you enroll</h1>
<EsyohWidget label="Programs accepting applicants now" intro="Accredited nutrition and dietetics programs currently taking applications." />
      <p class="lede">
        {resources.length} long-form guides from our team. Each one takes a position, supports it with data, and names
        the source. If we disagree with the conventional advice we say so and show you why.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <AiSummary>
        NutritionSchools.org publishes {resources.length} long-form guides on nutrition and dietetics education and
        careers, covering the difference between nutrition and dietetics, the step by step pathway to the RDN
        credential, what nutrition degree jobs actually exist, whether a nutrition degree is worth it, whether online
        nutrition degrees are respected, a full salary guide, and a sports nutrition career guide. Every guide is built
        on Bureau of Labor Statistics wage and projection data, our database of {stats.programs} programs at
        {' '}{stats.schools} institutions, and our own {outcomesSurvey.name} of {outcomesSurvey.sampleLabel}, which found
        {' '}{outcomesSurvey.headline.employedWithinSixMonths} percent employed within six months and
        {' '}{outcomesSurvey.headline.supervisedPracticeCritical} percent calling supervised practice critical to their
        career. Each guide is reviewed by a named credentialed member of our team and states its limitations. Last
        reviewed {site.reviewedLabel}.
      </AiSummary>

      <div class="hot-take">
        <strong>Guides that take a position are more useful than guides that do not</strong>
        <p>
          Neutral career advice is usually marketing that refused to sign its name. Each guide here argues something:
          the RDN is not optional for clinical work, online is not easier, sports nutrition is the most romanticized
          path in the field, and a nutrition degree without supervised practice is an expensive hobby. If you disagree,
          the data is on the page so you can.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="card" href="/resources/nutrition-career-outcomes/" style="margin-bottom:28px;display:block">
        <span class="label">Original research</span>
        <h3>Nutrition and Dietetics Career Outcomes Survey 2026</h3>
        <p>
          {outcomesSurvey.sampleLabel}. {outcomesSurvey.headline.employedWithinSixMonths} percent employed within six
          months. Starting salaries by credential, first career paths, skills in demand, and the limitations attached.
        </p>
        <span class="text-link">Read the survey →</span>
      </a>

      <div class="grid">
        {resources.map(resource => {
          const author = teamBySlug[resource.author] ?? site.team[0];
          return (
            <a class="card" href={`/resources/${resource.slug}/`}>
              <span class="label">{resource.kicker}</span>
              <h3>{resource.title}</h3>
              <p>{resource.summary}</p>
              <span class="text-link">Read the guide →</span>
              <p style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);margin:12px 0 0">Reviewed by {author.name}</p>
            </a>
          );
        })}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="content wrap">
    <h2>How we write these guides</h2>
    <p>
      Every guide separates four things and labels them. Facts an institution publishes about itself. Accreditation
      records from ACEND and the Commission on Dietetic Registration. Federal data, cited by release and date. And our
      own editorial opinion, which is marked as opinion rather than smuggled in as fact.
    </p>
    <p>
      That structure exists because most nutrition education content on the internet blends all four, which makes it
      impossible to check and therefore useless for a decision that costs six figures. If you can tell which sentence is
      a measurement and which is a judgement, you can disagree with the judgement and keep the measurement.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every guide is reviewed by a named member of our team who holds a relevant credential, and the reviewer appears at
      the top and bottom of the page. You can read their qualifications on the
      {' '}<a class="text-link" href="/about/">about page</a>, and the standards we hold ourselves to are on the
      {' '}<a class="text-link" href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>If you do not yet know whether you want dietetics or nutrition, read <a class="text-link" href="/resources/nutrition-vs-dietetics-whats-the-difference/">the field comparison</a> first. It is the fork that determines everything else.</li>
      <li>If you have decided on the credential, read <a class="text-link" href="/resources/how-to-become-a-registered-dietitian-step-by-step/">the RDN pathway</a> and then check the <a class="text-link" href="/rankings/best-nutrition-masters-programs/">masters rankings</a>.</li>
      <li>If you are weighing the money, read <a class="text-link" href="/resources/nutrition-salary-guide-2026/">the salary guide</a> and <a class="text-link" href="/resources/is-nutrition-degree-worth-it/">the return on investment analysis</a>.</li>
      <li>If online study is your only realistic option, read <a class="text-link" href="/resources/online-nutrition-degrees-are-they-respected/">the online degree guide</a>, which is mostly about supervised practice rather than about format.</li>
      <li>If you want the graduate outcomes in one place, read the <a class="text-link" href="/resources/nutrition-career-outcomes/">Career Outcomes Survey 2026</a> and then the <a class="text-link" href="/research/">full research record</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
<EsyohWidget label="Compare accredited programs" intro="Explore accredited nutrition and dietetics programs before you decide." />
</BaseLayout>
